     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've recorded the run as UNKNOWN: the installed sensors look normal, but I can't confirm the tube atmosphere without the pressure gauge, so I proposed calling a human.\n\n- **What looks normal:** Temperature followed the ramp, briefly went up to 760.5 °C and now holds at 750 °C. Oxygen is low (about 5–8 ppm), argon flow is steady at about 100 sccm, and heater power is steady at about 46%.\n- **What that doesn't settle:** Low oxygen argues against a seal leak. But a blocked exhaust would mainly show up as rising pressure, and nothing measures pressure here.\n- **Sample:** There are no measurements of the sample yet, so there's no evidence on whether the material grew.\n\nTo settle it I'd need a pressure reading during growth (for example, a manual check by the operator), then measurements of the sample after the run."
     }
